// Chapter 4 — the endings. Shows faction gates, triggers (guild-wary in story.talewright.yaml),
// conditional diverts and several endings.

=== ending.return
@title The Return

The walk back to camp is quiet. {guide:first-name} keeps glancing at your pack.

{if not (player has relic)}
-> ending.empty-handed
{/if}

* [Hand the relic to the guild] (requires: faction:explorers-guild >= neutral) { take player relic; faction:explorers-guild += 20 } -> ending.guild
* [Keep it for yourself] { faction:explorers-guild -= 30 } -> ending.keep

=== ending.guild
@title Honoured

The {faction:explorers-guild:name} hangs {player:last-name#possessive} portrait in the great hall, a little
crooked. Your standing with them is now *{faction:explorers-guild:tier#lower}*.
{if visited(dream.sleeper)}
{if flag:dream-promise}
You also deliver {archivist:first-name#possessive} testimony. The guild can no longer pretend it never sent anyone inside.
{else}
You keep the dream out of the report. The two remaining glyph marks stay locked in your desk.
{/if}
{/if}
{if player has idol}
Nobody asks about the {item:idol} on your desk.
{/if}
-> END

=== ending.keep
@title The Keeper

You keep the {item:relic}. It keeps you, too: you sleep less, and dream of a door with a closed eye.
{if visited(dream.sleeper)}
{if player:lucidity >= 5}
You remember {sleeper:first-name#possessive} warning clearly. When the door appears, you know not to open it.
{else}
The warning returns in fragments. You count your two remaining glyph marks until morning.
{/if}
{else}
{if visited(dream.arrival)}
You wonder what waited beyond the dream you abandoned.
{/if}
{/if}
{if flag:guild-wary}
The guild's letters stop coming. Then the guild's people start coming instead.
// Nested conditionals and a compound and/or test. Blocks nest up to 64 levels; `and` binds tighter than `or`,
// and parentheses group as usual.
{if player:level >= 2 and (player has idol or visited(temple.side))}
You meet them at the door, rested and unhurried{if player has idol}, the {item:idol} watching from the
mantel behind you{/if}. They leave without the relic, and never quite work out why.
{else}
You start sleeping with the relic under your pillow.
{/if}
{/if}
-> END

=== ending.empty-handed
@title Empty-Handed

You return with nothing but {player:pronoun:possessive-pronoun:determiner} notes and a story nobody at the guild quite
believes. {guide:first-name}, at least, buys you a drink.
{if visited(dream.sleeper)}
You left the {item:relic}, but not the memory of {sleeper:first-name}.
{if flag:dream-promise and faction:explorers-guild >= friendly}
The guild ghost's testimony earns a hearing, even without treasure.
{else}
The glyph marks are proof enough for the two of you.
{/if}
{/if}
-> END
